---

<ApplicationLayout
  hideBottomCTA={true}
  title="Alfa Laval WHPX 513 Self-Cleaning, Diesel Fuel Oil Centrifuge"
  disableTitleSuffix={true}
  description="Alfa Laval WHPX 513 partial-discharge centrifuge. Diesel application capacity: 16,400 L/h (72.21 US GPM) at 13 cSt and 40 C. Exact HFO capacity data included."
  category="products"
  categoryLabel="Products"
  categoryHref="/alfa-laval-centrifuges/"
  heroImage="/images/alfa-laval-whpx-513/Alfa_Laval_WHPX-513_70_GPM_Centrifuge_Wastewater_Plant.png"
  heroImageAlt="Alfa Laval WHPX 513 Self-Cleaning Centrifuge System"
  canonicalUrl="https://dolphincentrifuge.com/alfa-laval-whpx-513/"
  jsonLd={jsonLd}
  toc={toc}
  relatedApplications={relatedApplications}
>

  <h3 id="overview">Overview</h3>

  <p>The Alfa Laval WHPX 513 Centrifuge is a self-cleaning <a href="/disc-stack-centrifuge/">disc-stack centrifuge</a> built for the three-phase separation of mixed fluids and sludge.</p>

  <p>With a 15 HP motor, the WHPX 513 has a published marine-diesel application capacity of 16,400 L/h (72.21 US GPM) at 13 cSt and a centrifugation temperature of 40 &deg;C.</p>

  <p>Dolphin Centrifuge is the independent specialist in Alfa Laval centrifuges, with remanufactured machines, turnkey systems, parts, and service built on 40+ years of Alfa Laval experience. Dolphin packages this machine as the DMPX-070 module, a Dolphin system built around a remanufactured Alfa Laval WHPX 513. Dolphin is an independent remanufacturer and is not affiliated with Alfa Laval.</p>

  <h3 id="application">Application</h3>

  <p>The Alfa Laval WHPX 513 Centrifuge is widely used in marine and industrial applications. Some of these applications are:</p>

  <ul>
    <li><strong><a href="/alfa-laval-diesel-centrifuge/">Diesel Fuel</a></strong></li>
    <li><a href="/black-diesel-centrifuge/"><strong>Black Diesel</strong></a></li>
    <li><strong><a href="/fuel-oil-centrifuge/">Intermediate and Heavy Fuel Oils (IFO, HFO)</a></strong></li>
    <li><strong><a href="/waste-oil-centrifuge/">Waste Oil</a></strong></li>
    <li><strong><a href="/machine-coolant-centrifuge/">Industrial Fluids &amp; Machining Coolants</a></strong></li>
    <li><strong><a href="/lube-oil-centrifuge/">Lubricating Oils</a></strong>.</li>
  </ul>

  <figure>
    <img
      src="/images/alfa-laval-whpx-513/Stainless_Steel_WHPX-513_Centrifuge_Module_for_WVO_Purification.webp"
      alt="Alfa Laval WHPX 513 Stainless Steel Centrifuge Module for WVO Purification"
      width="500"
      height="500"
      loading="lazy"
      class="img-cap-500"
    />
    <figcaption>Alfa Laval WHPX 513 Centrifuge System with Feed Pump, Sludge Tank</figcaption>
  </figure>

  <h3 id="whpx-513-specifications">Specifications</h3>

  <div class="not-prose overflow-x-auto border border-gray-100 rounded-xl">
    <table>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>Model Type</td><td>Alfa Laval WHPX 513 TGD 24-60</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Diesel Application Capacity</td><td>16,400 L/h (72.21 US GPM) at 13 cSt and 40 &deg;C</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Rated Reference Capacity</td><td>24,500 L/h (107.87 US GPM); source fluid not specified</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Sludge Space</td><td>3.87 Gallons</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Motor HP:</td><td>15 HP</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Voltages:</td><td>230 / 460 V, 3 phase</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <p>The rated reference value is published without a process-fluid identity. It is not a diesel, water, wastewater, or other application capacity. Application capacity must stay attached to the exact fluid, viscosity, and centrifugation temperature.</p>

  <h3 id="whpx-513-capacity-data">Published WHPX 513 Capacity Data</h3>

  <div class="not-prose overflow-x-auto border border-gray-100 rounded-xl mb-6">
    <table class="w-full text-sm">
      <thead>
        <tr><th>Fluid</th><th>Published capacity</th><th>Derived US GPM</th><th>Conditions</th></tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>Marine diesel</td><td>16,400 L/h</td><td>72.21</td><td>13 cSt at 40 &deg;C; centrifugation at 40 &deg;C</td></tr>
        <tr><td>HFO, 30 cSt at 50 &deg;C</td><td>15,200 L/h</td><td>66.92</td><td>Centrifugation at 70-98 &deg;C</td></tr>
        <tr><td>HFO, 40 cSt at 50 &deg;C</td><td>15,200 L/h</td><td>66.92</td><td>Centrifugation at 80-98 &deg;C</td></tr>
        <tr><td>HFO, 60 cSt at 50 &deg;C</td><td>11,500 L/h</td><td>50.63</td><td>Centrifugation at 80-98 &deg;C</td></tr>
        <tr><td>HFO, 100 cSt at 50 &deg;C</td><td>11,000 L/h</td><td>48.43</td><td>Centrifugation at 90-98 &deg;C</td></tr>
        <tr><td>HFO, 180 cSt at 50 &deg;C</td><td>7,600 L/h</td><td>33.46</td><td>Centrifugation at 90-98 &deg;C</td></tr>
        <tr><td>HFO, 380 cSt at 50 &deg;C</td><td>6,400 L/h</td><td>28.18</td><td>Centrifugation at 98 &deg;C</td></tr>
        <tr><td>HFO, 460 cSt at 50 &deg;C</td><td>5,400 L/h</td><td>23.78</td><td>Centrifugation at 98 &deg;C</td></tr>
        <tr><td>HFO, 600 cSt at 50 &deg;C</td><td>4,400 L/h</td><td>19.37</td><td>Centrifugation at 98 &deg;C</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Cross-head R&amp;O lube oil</td><td>7,400-8,600 L/h</td><td>32.58-37.86</td><td>Centrifugation at 80-90 &deg;C</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Cross-head detergent lube oil</td><td>7,400-8,100 L/h</td><td>32.58-35.66</td><td>Centrifugation at 80-90 &deg;C</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Trunk detergent lube oil</td><td>4,400-5,400 L/h</td><td>19.37-23.78</td><td>Centrifugation at 80-90 &deg;C</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Steam turbine lube oil</td><td>15,900 L/h</td><td>70.01</td><td>Centrifugation at 60-70 &deg;C</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <p>The source cell for cross-head detergent lube oil lists its endpoints as 8,100-7,400 L/h; the table above normalizes them to ascending order while the machine-readable record preserves the original cell text. US GPM values are derived from L/h using L/h &divide; 227.124707 and rounded to two decimals. See the <a href="/technical-data/">technical data methodology</a> or the <a href="/technical-data/alfa-laval-whpx-513.json">WHPX 513 machine-readable record</a>.</p>

  <div class="bg-navy/5 border-l-4 border-gold/40 rounded-r-lg p-4 my-6 not-prose">
    <p class="text-sm text-text-light leading-relaxed">If you have simple, routine questions: We have condensed our 40+ years of disc-stack centrifuge experience into <a href="/disc-stack-centrifuge-faq/" class="text-navy font-semibold underline hover:text-gold">101 Frequently Asked Questions about Disc Stack Centrifuges</a>!</p>
  </div>

  <h2 id="fopx-613">Alfa Laval FOPX 613 TFD Partial-Discharge Disc-Stack Centrifuge</h2>

  <p>The Alfa Laval FOPX 613 Centrifuge is a self-cleaning disc-stack centrifuge specially built for the three-phase separation of fuel oils, such as <a href="/fuel-oil-centrifuge/">heavy fuel oil</a> (HFO). The <strong>FO </strong>in FOPX stands for <strong>F</strong>uel <strong>O</strong>il.</p>

  <p>With a 15 HP Motor, the FOPX 613 centrifuge has a bowl RPM of 4,100 and can process 30 GPM of ISO 380 cSt Heavy Fuel Oil.</p>

